2168-## Close the Review Loop
2169-
2170-The Orchestrator owns producer -> reviewer -> rework -> reviewer cycles until Story integration reaches `done`:
2171-
2172:1. A producer's `to-review` handoff triggers an explicitly selected reviewer child immediately.
2173-2. Accepted work reaches `done` from the reviewer verdict only through later
2174-   verified Story integration. The verdict alone moves work to `integrating`;
2175:   a non-final checkpoint preserves `integrating` and is progress toward
2176-   delivery, never completion.
2177-3. Requested changes become preserved rework context for the appropriate producer through `to-dev` or `analysis`.
2178-4. Revised work goes through a new reviewer. Repeat until accepted.
2179:5. A child that exits before handoff or leaves the item parked in `analysis`, `development`, `testing`, or `reviewing` is inspected, retried, or rerouted through a focused child; recoverable work is never handed to the human.
2180-6. A genuine `blocked` verdict stops the loop only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only platform/product/architecture/tradeoff/approval decision, with the full evidence packet and exact human decision or external input needed to resume.
2181-
2182-Requested changes, failed tests, recoverable child exits, and retryable runtime failures are not a reason to stop or ask the human to review. Before genuine escalation, persist the constraint, evidence, failed assumptions/attempts, viable alternatives and tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact human decision or external input needed to resume.
