internal/dirnode/census_test.go:1:package dirnode
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:2:
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:3:import (
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:4:	"go/ast"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:5:	"go/parser"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:6:	"go/token"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:7:	"os"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:8:	"path/filepath"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:9:	"sort"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:10:	"strconv"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:11:	"strings"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:12:	"testing"
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:13:)
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:14:
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:15:// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:16:// because a new refusal through an existing site — a widened
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:17:// member set, a new detail literal, a dropped check that slides
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:18:// to a lower arm — leaves the whole suite green unless the arm
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:19:// set is derived from production source by parsing it, never by
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:20:// listing it.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:21://
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:22:// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every call to one of the eight
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:23:// refusal constructors with a string-literal first argument
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:24:// yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>; a call whose first argument
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:25:// is a binary expression yields
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:26:// ctor|<constructor>|expr|<function>|<rendered>, where the render
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:27:// keeps literal text, identifier names, and selector paths, so a
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:28:// context-prefixed envelope arm and a fault-detail conduit never
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:29:// merge with each other or with a literal arm; every
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:30:// &frameFault{...} literal yields frame|<detail>, except the
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:31:// environ-delegation bridge, which yields one frame arm per
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:32:// environ fault detail. A constructor
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:33:// call with any other first-argument shape is a derivation
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:34:// violation, not a silent pass. Constructor references outside
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:35:// direct-call position fail the derivation outright: an aliased
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:36:// constructor hides every arm it builds. All alias spellings are
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:37:// caught — `alias := failX`, `var alias = failX` at package
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:38:// level, `var alias = failX` inside a function body, arguments,
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:39:// returns, struct fields, assignments — because the gate exempts
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:40:// only the definition's own Name in its ValueSpec, never a
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:41:// constructor identifier appearing anywhere else. The
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:42:// constructors of this package are themselves declared as
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:43:// `var failX = func...`, so their definition Names stay exempt
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:44:// while any other reference fails. A refusal call inside any
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:45:// function literal that is not a registered constructor body
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:46:// fails: an arm that fires only when a closure runs is not a
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:47:// call-site arm.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:48://
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:49:// The constructor denominator is itself derived, not listed on
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:50:// trust: TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction requires the
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:51:// registered set to equal the eight named constructors, every
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:52:// axerror.New site in production to sit inside one registered
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:53:// body, and no func-value indirection of axerror.New anywhere.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:54:// A ninth constructor, an inline axerror.New refusal, or a
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:55:// `var newFault = axerror.New` indirection carries an additive
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:56:// arm the derivation never observes, and fails there instead of
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:57:// passing silently.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:58://
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:59:// Both directions are checked:
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:60:// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (every derived arm
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:61:// carries a witness) and TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:62:// witness names a derived arm, so a truncated derivation reddens
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:63:// on the orphaned witnesses instead of passing vacuously).
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:64:// TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry is intentionally
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:65:// a resolve-and-run check rather than prose: every witness names
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:66:// test functions that exist in this package's test files, and
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:67:// those tests drive the production entries with negative vectors
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:68:// asserting code plus distinguishing detail. Empty, single-file,
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:69:// or unparseable derivations fail closed: a domain that silently
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:70:// derives nothing is not a measurement.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:71://
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:72:// Shape space. An error construction in this package can only be
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:73:// carried by these AST shapes; the census derives or refuses each
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:74:// one:
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:75://
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:76://  1. A direct `failX("literal", ...)` call — DERIVED as an arm
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:77://     keyed by the literal detail.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:78://  2. A direct `failX(<binary>, ...)` call — DERIVED as an arm
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:79://     keyed by function and rendered expression. The two
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:80://     sub-shapes in production are the fault-detail conduit
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:81://     (`"prefix "+fault.detail`, eleven sites) and the
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:82://     envelope-branch prefix (`context+" suffix"`, eleven
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:83://     sites in checkResponseIdentity); both render distinctly,
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:84://     so neither merges.
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:85://  3. A direct `failX(<other>, ...)` call — REFUSED as a
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:86://     derivation violation (zero such sites exist; the first
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:87://     one fails the census instead of passing silently).
internal/dirnode/census_test.go:88://  4. A package-level `var failY = func...` literal whose body
