internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:9:// This file pins vector reachability against the arm-slide shape
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:10:// (review round 2, B3): a negative vector carrying two defects is
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:11:// satisfied by whichever arm fires first, and when both arms share
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:12:// the same code the code assertion cannot tell them apart. The
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:13:// unknown_field vector did exactly this — it inserted a duplicate
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:14:// "fields" member, so decodeStrictObject refused on the duplicate
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:15:// before the field registry ever ran, with the same code and the
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:16:// same detail either path reports.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:17://
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:18:// The audit covered every fixture-surgery vector in this package
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:19:// that claims a "missing" or "unknown" outcome:
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:20://
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:21://   - query "missing caller", manifest "missing member", and probe
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:22://     response "missing member" all renamed the member (",\"x\":" to
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:23://     ",\"xX\":"). Renaming fires the unknown-member arm first
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:24://     because every envelope checks unknownMember before
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:25://     missingMember, so the missing arm carried a witness that
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:26://     never fired it. All three now delete the member instead, and
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:27://     TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm asserts the
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:28://     misses-a-required-member message, which a rename vector
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:29://     cannot produce.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:30://   - scan request/response "missing member" vectors already
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:31://     delete and probe request "missing member" already deletes.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:32://     The "unknown member" vectors are NOT audited here at all:
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:33://     three of them named the envelope unknown-member arm while
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:34://     reaching a strict-decode, operation, and node-build arm
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:35://     (review round 3, C1), so a prose claim that each reaches
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:36://     the arm it names is exactly the failure mode.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:37://     Vector reachability is derived instead, in
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:38://     arm_reachability_test.go: every envelope unknown/missing
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:39://     vector is paired with its arm key, and the test computes
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:40://     the reached arm from the refusal message and fails when
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:41://     that is not the named one.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:42://   - the operation-level query vectors (unknown operation,
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:43://     parameter, filter, field, preset, sort, flag, pagination)
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:44://     all collapse to the single checkQueryOperation arm by
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:45://     construction; their obligation set is derived and driven
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:46://     member-by-member in query_operations_test.go rather than
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:47://     distinguished by a detail production does not emit.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:48:
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:49:// TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm requires the three
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:50:// deletion-built missing vectors to refuse with the missing-member
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:51:// message through the production entry. A rename-built vector
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:52:// would report "carries unknown member" here and fail, so this
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:53:// test pins the construction, not just the code.
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:54:func TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm(t *testing.T) {
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:55:	t.Parallel()
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:56:	t.Run("query missing caller", func(t *testing.T) {
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:57:		t.Parallel()
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:58:		body := replaceOnce(t, fixtureQueryJSON(), `,"caller":`+fixtureCallerJSON(), ``, 1)
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:59:		_, err := DecodeQuery([]byte(body))
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:60:		failure := requireCode(t, err, "query_invalid")
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:61:		if !strings.Contains(failure.Message(), "misses a required member") {
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:62:			t.Fatalf("message = %q, want the missing-member arm, not the unknown-member arm", failure.Message())
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:63:		}
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:64:	})
internal/dirnode/arm_identity_test.go:65:	t.Run("manifest missing member", func(t *testing.T) {
