internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:1:package dirnode
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:2:
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:3:// This file is the bound census (review round 2, B1), ported from
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:4:// the sessadapter leaf's bound_census_test.go. It exists because a
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:5:// new bound through any of the eight helpers — checkStringBounds,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:6:// checkUint53Bounds, checkSortedUniqueStrings,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:7:// checkSortedUniqueDigests, checkSortedUniqueUUIDv7,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:8:// checkEnumSubset, checkUUIDv7DigestSubset, checkOptionalString —
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:9:// or a new explicit len(...) guard passes every behavioral test
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:10:// that never names it, and pinning checkStringBounds while the
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:11:// query validators go unmeasured reads as complete while most of
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:12:// the class stays open: the same checkStringBounds max+1 mutant
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:13:// killed in sessadapter survived on every maximum checked here.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:14://
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:15:// Shape, modelled on TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered:
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:16:// scanBoundSiteIDs derives every bound site from production source
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:17:// (helper calls with their member, len guards in any statement
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:18:// context), and TestBoundGuardsAreCensused requires the derived
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:19:// multiset to equal boundRegistrations exactly. A new bound in one
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:20:// of the derived shapes below with no row fails the census; a
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:21:// removed bound orphans its row and fails too. A helper alias
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:22:// (`var f = checkStringBounds`) fails as an indirection violation
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:23:// rather than a missed site. An empty scan fails closed. Site
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:24:// identity is file|function|member, never the bound values: a
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:25:// moved bound (+1) keeps its identity and must redden its
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:26:// behavioral driver, which the mutant battery proves per row.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:27://
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:28:// Shape space. A bound in this package can only be carried by
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:29:// these AST shapes; the census derives the marked ones and bounds
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:30:// the rest:
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:31://
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:32://   1. A direct call to one of the eight helpers — DERIVED with
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:33://      the bounded member.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:34://   2. A bound helper through a func-value indirection (var,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:35://      :=, assignment, argument, return, struct field, method
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:36://      value) — DERIVED as a census violation (the alias
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:37://      itself fails rather than each hidden call).
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:38://   3. A comparison holding a len(...) call in any statement
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:39://      context (if, for, switch, return, assignment) — DERIVED.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:40://   4. A comparison over a length variable bound from len(...)
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:41://      or stringLength(...) (`n := len(v); if n > 4096`) —
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:42://      DERIVED; live mechanism rows are the shared
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:43://      character-count enforcements in checkStringBounds,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:44://      checkSortedUniqueStrings, and checkURI.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:45://   5. A comparison holding a direct stringLength(...) call —
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:46://      DERIVED by the same rule; live instance:
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:47://      CheckCursorReuse.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:48://   6. A bound inside a package-level var initializer,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:49://      including func literals — DERIVED under the variable
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:50://      name; zero live rows today, proven by the synthetic
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:51://      package-literal test below.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:52://   7. A comparison over a decoded value or caller-supplied
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:53://      number with no length source in the function
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:54://      (`skip > 1000000` over a rawUint53 result, `deadlineMS <
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:55://      MinDeadlineMS` over a plain parameter, `index > 63`,
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:56://      `take < 1`, `version != 1`, cross-field gates) — STATED
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:57://      BOUND, not derived. Each is pinned behaviourally by its
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:58://      named driver; the bound is enforced at the entry the
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:59://      driver drives.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:60://   8. The maxUint53 maxima — STATED: representability bounds
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:61://      pinned once by TestUint53RepresentabilityCeiling rather
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:62://      than per site.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:63://   9. A direct cap(...) or utf8.RuneCountInString(...)
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:64://      comparison outside stringLength — STATED BOUND, not
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:65://      derived. No live instance: the only production
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:66://      rune-count use is inside stringLength, whose callers are
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:67://      all rostered rows.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:68://  10. An ordering comparison with no length source
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:69://      (`previous >= record.Key` in Journal.Import, pairwise
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:70://      sortedness scans `values[index-1] >= values[index]`) —
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:71://      STATED, not derived: ordering gates, not domain bounds.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:72://      Both halves are pinned behaviourally: the sortedness
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:73://      refusal tests feed unsorted vectors (["b","a"]) for the
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:74://      ordered half, and TestSortedUniqueDuplicatesRefuse feeds a
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:75://      duplicate at every one of the eight scans for the
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:76://      uniqueness half — a duplicate is sorted, so only it proves
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:77://      the `>=` (not `>`) comparison.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:78://
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:79:// 6 of 10 shapes derived, 4 stated. A new bound in shapes 1-6
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:80:// with no row fails TestBoundGuardsAreCensused; shapes 7-10 are
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:81:// pinned by their named suites or stated here as residue.
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:82://
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:83:// Every non-exempt row names its driver: the committed test
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:84:// proving refusal at its edges (min-1/max+1) through the
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:85:// production entry. Admission at the accepted edge itself is
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:86:// proven only where the driver says so. Exempt rows say why:
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:87:// equivalent (the bound is unreachable behind an upstream gate),
internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go:88:// mechanism (transparent forwarder or generic guard whose values
