internal/dirnode/doc.go:1:// Package dirnode implements the ax host side of the companion
internal/dirnode/doc.go:2:// Directory Node protocol of pinned specification Section 7.9: the
internal/dirnode/doc.go:3:// two-major bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest and probe
internal/dirnode/doc.go:4:// validation, scan/inventory request framing with (operation,
internal/dirnode/doc.go:5:// operation_id) idempotency, Session Directory Query framing of
internal/dirnode/doc.go:6:// Section 10.8.5, façade binding checks, and Structured Error
internal/dirnode/doc.go:7:// 1.2.0 refusals.
internal/dirnode/doc.go:8://
internal/dirnode/doc.go:9:// The actor every Section 7.9 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax
internal/dirnode/doc.go:10:// host (this repository). The directory node is a child surface this
internal/dirnode/doc.go:11:// package never trusts: it runs in the same per-environment
internal/dirnode/doc.go:12:// implementation as Provider 2 and Session Adapter 1, and every byte
internal/dirnode/doc.go:13:// it emits is attacker-influenced, so every frame is validated
internal/dirnode/doc.go:14:// before any member is used. Neither major adds operations to
internal/dirnode/doc.go:15:// Provider 2, executes Continuation Plans, or transports
internal/dirnode/doc.go:16:// transcript/workspace bytes, and this host never asks for any of
internal/dirnode/doc.go:17:// those through this package.
internal/dirnode/doc.go:18://
internal/dirnode/doc.go:19:// Major negotiation is caller-driven enumeration, not a hello: the
internal/dirnode/doc.go:20:// caller attempts its locally supported majors in strictly
internal/dirnode/doc.go:21:// descending order with one manifest request each, each attempt on a
internal/dirnode/doc.go:22:// fresh process. Only the exact downgrade tuple — one well-framed
internal/dirnode/doc.go:23:// failure echoing the request, response schema_version 1.0.0,
internal/dirnode/doc.go:24:// Structured Error 1.2 incompatible_protocol with exit 6 and
internal/dirnode/doc.go:25:// retryable=false, then process exit 6 — authorizes the next lower
internal/dirnode/doc.go:26:// attempt. Deciding that tuple is DecideBootstrapStep; launching and
internal/dirnode/doc.go:27:// reaping processes belongs to the caller, which records each
internal/dirnode/doc.go:28:// attempt's process token in a ProcessGuard so a returned or failed
internal/dirnode/doc.go:29:// process is never reused for a lower major.
internal/dirnode/doc.go:30://
internal/dirnode/doc.go:31:// A failed read is never an absence: a partial, malformed,
internal/dirnode/doc.go:32:// over-limit, mislabeled, or escaped result is an
internal/dirnode/doc.go:33:// adapter_protocol_violation or transport_failure, never an empty
internal/dirnode/doc.go:34:// result and never fallback permission. A syntactically valid frame
internal/dirnode/doc.go:35:// naming an unknown operation is operation_unknown, refused
internal/dirnode/doc.go:36:// locally before any node surface is touched. Query framing
internal/dirnode/doc.go:37:// defects are query_invalid.
internal/dirnode/doc.go:38://
internal/dirnode/doc.go:39:// Stated bounds: transport process management (spawning the node
internal/dirnode/doc.go:40:// executable, deadlines, stdio ownership, allowlist/SSH admission)
internal/dirnode/doc.go:41:// belongs to the caller, which supplies frames this package
internal/dirnode/doc.go:42:// validates as bytes; the content of nested observation and lineage
internal/dirnode/doc.go:43:// types owned by Sections 10.8 and 13.14 (EnvironmentObservation,
internal/dirnode/doc.go:44:// NativeSessionObservation, InventoryBatch, PreviewExcerpt payload
internal/dirnode/doc.go:45:// meaning, EnrichmentJobRequest/Receipt chains, ManagementBinding
internal/dirnode/doc.go:46:// content, RuntimeExpectation) is checked for presence and object
internal/dirnode/doc.go:47:// shape only — the shared-environment leaf of this Story owns that
internal/dirnode/doc.go:48:// content, and inventing its validation here would collide with that
internal/dirnode/doc.go:49:// ownership at integration. The scan journal in this package is an
internal/dirnode/doc.go:50:// in-memory (operation, operation_id) record with byte export and
internal/dirnode/doc.go:51:// import so crash recovery is demonstrable; its durable placement is
internal/dirnode/doc.go:52:// the core's property. Caller authentication (CallerContext is
internal/dirnode/doc.go:53:// authenticated server-side, never accepted from an unverified body
internal/dirnode/doc.go:54:// alone) belongs to the caller: this package validates the context
internal/dirnode/doc.go:55:// shape. Section 10.8.5 prose names a query_cursor_mismatch code the
internal/dirnode/doc.go:56:// pinned error registry does not register; cursor reuse after a
internal/dirnode/doc.go:57:// bound change is refused here as query_invalid with a
internal/dirnode/doc.go:58:// cursor-mismatch detail, and the divergence is recorded on the
internal/dirnode/doc.go:59:// refusing call site, not hidden.
internal/dirnode/doc.go:60:package dirnode
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:1:package dirnode
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:2:
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:3:import (
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:4:	"bytes"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:5:	"encoding/json"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:6:
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:7:	"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:8:	"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:9:)
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:10:
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:11:// Wire constants of pinned specification Section 7.9. Directory
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:12:// Node protocol 2.0.0 is the current separately negotiated
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:13:// read-mostly façade; 1.0.0 remains an immutable legacy wire
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:14:// contract. Neither major is a negotiation: a different major is an
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:15:// invalid envelope, never a downgrade, except through the exact
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:16:// manifest downgrade tuple DecideBootstrapStep recognizes.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:17:const (
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:18:	// ProtocolID is the exact protocol member every request and
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:19:	// response envelope carries.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:20:	ProtocolID = "urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:21:	// RequestSchema is the exact schema member every request
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:22:	// envelope carries.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:23:	RequestSchema = "urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-request"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:24:	// ResponseSchema is the exact schema member every response
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:25:	// envelope carries. The response carries its own schema
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:26:	// member because the downgrade tuple names a response
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:27:	// schema_version distinct from every echoed request member;
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:28:	// a response without one cannot carry that tuple.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:29:	ResponseSchema = "urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-response"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:30:	// ManifestSchema is the exact schema identifier the manifest
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:31:	// body carries.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:32:	ManifestSchema = "urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-manifest"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:33:	// ManifestSchemaVersion is the only manifest version this host
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:34:	// accepts under either major.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:35:	ManifestSchemaVersion = "1.0.0"
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:36:	// ResponseSchemaVersion is the only response schema_version
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:37:	// this host accepts under either major: both majors bind
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:38:	// Directory Node Response 1.0.0.
internal/dirnode/protocol.go:39:	ResponseSchemaVersion = "1.0.0"
