internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:12:
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:13:// This file is the derived arm-reachability gate (review round 3,
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:14:// C1). The arm census in census_test.go derives every refusal arm
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:15:// from production source and maps each to witness tests, but it
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:16:// never checks that a witness actually fires the arm it names: a
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:17:// vector carrying two defects is satisfied by whichever arm fires
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:18:// first, and three committed "unknown member" vectors proved this
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:19:// by reaching a strict-decode, operation, and node-build arm while
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:20:// naming the envelope unknown-member arm. A code-only assertion
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:21:// cannot tell those paths apart, and a deleted-member vector
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:22:// refuses downstream with the same code, so code-only witnesses
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:23:// leave missing-member, extensions, and empty-frame arms deletable
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:24:// with a green suite.
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:25://
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:26:// The gate below closes the class without another hand audit.
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:27:// Every row pairs one production-derived arm key with a vector
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:28:// driven through a production entry, and the test computes which
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:29:// arm the vector actually reaches from the refusal message:
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:30://
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:31://   - a literal arm (ctor|<ctor>|<detail>) matches when the message
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:32://     carries its full detail; the row passes only when exactly the
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:33://     named literal matches, so a vector that slides to a sibling
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:34://     arm or to the strict conduit fails naming the arm it reached;
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:35://   - a fault conduit (..."<prefix> "+fault.detail) or a
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:36://     context-prefixed arm (context+"<suffix>") matches on its
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:37://     derived prefix/suffix; the row passes only when the named arm
internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go:38://     matches, no literal matches, and every other match is at most
