+# Mesh RPC 2 namespace inventory
+
+`internal/merkleinventory` builds deterministic Merkle roots and child bodies
+for the six Mesh RPC 2 namespaces, validates immutable schema membership and
+serves bounded `inventory.roots`, `inventory.children` and `objects.get`
+requests. The node encoding uses the RFC 8785 implementation in
+`internal/canonicaljson` and Section 11.4 domain
+`urn:ax:merkle-node:1`.
+
+The schema table contains 19 included schema/version pairs and 42 known
+excluded schema identities. A Blob Descriptor belongs to `manifest`, complete
+raw content belongs to `blob`, and a Chunk is transfer material with no
+inventory root. Local markers and transient request/response bodies are
+excluded. An unknown immutable schema fails closed. Descriptor-as-record,
+independent Chunk admission and a local marker are tested against both
+membership and roots.
+
+Four included rows still fail closed at `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity`
+because their complete shapes are not implemented there:
+`session-record@3.1.0`, `materialization-plan@1.0.0`,
+`materialization-plan@2.0.0`, and `task-board-bundle@1.0.0`. Their destination
+namespace is explicit in the mapping table, but `ClassifyJSON` does not admit
+them. `MIXED-NS-1` root fixtures use the specification's synthetic IDs through
+the production root entry; they do not claim that synthetic IDs can be
+recomputed from real object bytes.
+
+`Index` is process-local. It does not persist inventory state, open a network
+connection, transfer chunks, materialize content, mutate sessions, execute a
+Tombstone, or advertise an anti-entropy/Host Channel capability. The
+in-process exchange test validates Checkpoint and Descriptor admission,
+idempotent replay, Tombstone/Acknowledgement retention, different timestamps
+without winner selection, bounded recursive retrieval, record-before-blob
+ordering, and six literal post-exchange roots. The normative MIXED-NS-EXCHANGE
+asks those byte-validated objects to have synthetic IDs `Z(3)` and `T(2)` from
+MIXED-NS-1, but provides no bytes with those identities; producing matching
+canonical objects would require SHA-256 preimages. Its combined normative
+exchange fixture is therefore not claimed. Durable union,
+lease-head derivation, losing-lease-event preservation, network transport and
+Section 11.5 staging/recovery remain outside this package's entry points.
+
+`New` accepts Mesh RPC 2.0.0 only. Mesh RPC 3 and 4 add
+`directory_record` and `terminal_backend_evidence`; their schema classes are
+not RPC 2 exclusions. Mesh RPC 5 adds authenticated host dispatch
+requirements. These version-specific object and authority rules are refused
+or remain with their respective owners. The package is not wired into the
+authenticated Host Channel handler.
+
+## Commands and outputs
+
+From the repository root:
+
+| Purpose | Command | Output |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Package behavior | `go test ./internal/merkleinventory -count=1 -v` | Test output; task logs under `.temp/TASK-260830-nxqqaw/` |
+| Canonical identity and inventory behavior | `go test ./internal/canonicaljson ./internal/merkleinventory -count=1 -v` | Test output; task logs under `.temp/TASK-260830-nxqqaw/` |
+| Narrowing evidence | `python3 internal/merkleinventory/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-nxqqaw/mutations` | One overlay and raw test log per mutant, plus `results.json` and `table.md` |
+
+See [CONFORMANCE-MATRIX.md](CONFORMANCE-MATRIX.md) for the gate/entry axis
+census and [TRACEABILITY.md](TRACEABILITY.md) for clause-to-test bindings and
+measured bounds.
