@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Inventory implementation notes
+
+Task: `TASK-260830-nxqqaw`.
+
+## Authority and decision
+
+The implementation follows the embedded `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.
+Section 11.4's exact root/child fixtures are explicitly “Mesh RPC 2.0.0” and
+Section 11.3 gives that historical surface the six namespace bounds `[1..6]`.
+This leaf implements RPC 2 inventories only. Section 11.8 adds
+`directory_record` for RPC 3 and requires source-authority and disclosure gates;
+Section 11.9 adds `terminal_backend_evidence` for RPC 4 and retains those gates.
+Those extensions are outside this leaf. `rpcwire.Namespaces(version)` remains
+the vocabulary owner; the inventory entry refuses versions other than 2.0.0
+instead of accepting a later version while omitting its namespace semantics.
+Host Channel's current RPC 5 support is not an inventory support claim; the
+future operation owner must explicitly compose an inventory implementation
+for that negotiated major before dispatch.
+
+## Existing owners
+
+- `internal/rpcwire` validates request envelopes, `inventory.roots` namespace
+  requests, root response cardinality/order, and version vocabulary. The new
+  package calls those entries and does not fork those validators.
+- `internal/canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` validates the supported closed
+  immutable JSON shapes and computes omit-self identities. Inventory maps the
+  returned schema identity to one RPC 2 namespace.
+- Complete raw blobs are admitted only together with a schema-valid Blob
+  Descriptor whose `blob_id` equals the raw-byte SHA-256. Chunk data has no
+  entry point in the inventory builder and therefore cannot affect any root.
+
+## Known owner boundary
+
+`canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` currently recognizes Tombstone,
+Tombstone Acknowledgement, Materialization Plan, and Task-board Bundle identity
+fields but deliberately refuses their complete schema shapes. Inventory must
+fail closed for those JSON objects until the existing canonicaljson owner
+provides full validators. MIXED-NS-1's normative roots are still pinned as
+Merkle algorithm fixtures over the spec's explicitly synthetic, schema-labelled
+IDs; those fixture inputs are not used to claim that the four unavailable
+validators exist. This limitation and the moved-class importer consequences
+will be stated in the handoff evidence.
+
