+# TASK-260830-nxqqaw conformance matrix
+
+Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §10, §11.3, §11.4, and §11.5.
+The task record's v0.5.0 reference is stale; the producer instruction pins the
+v0.7.0 text. Base checkpoint: `360c8bd79cc2325ab661a9ba591b6bfb82ebe0ea`.
+Candidate remains uncommitted in the managed Story worktree. Fixtures use no
+network, wall clock, or durable storage.
+
+## Producer property results
+
+| Property | Result | Evidence and remaining bound |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Deterministic trie | Driven | `TestNormativeRootAndChildFixtures`, `TestDispatchServesNormativeChildrenBody`, `TestMixedNS1RootsFromNormativeSyntheticIDs`, and rule 4 depth sweep drive `Index.Root`, `Index.Child`, `ComputeNode`, and `Index.Dispatch`; isolated rule 1–5 narrowings are in the mutation run. |
+| Total, disjoint membership | Partial | The 19 included rows and 42 exclusions have a closed mapping test, descriptor/chunk/local-marker negatives, and cross-namespace `objects.get` refusal. Four included schemas still fail closed in `canonicaljson`: Session Record 3.1.0, Materialization Plan 1.0.0/2.0.0, and Task-board Bundle 1.0.0. |
+| Bounded serving | Driven | `Index.Dispatch` composes `rpcwire.DecodeRequest` / `EncodeSuccess`; namespace, prefix, response, and negotiated-line axes have named tests and narrowings. `FetchObjects` sends singleton batches under the line limit. |
+| Union exchange | Partial | Real validated objects are exchanged in process; the test pins only record/manifest/blob root changes, exact missing Checkpoint/Descriptor retrieval, and six literal final roots. Tombstone/Acknowledgement union retains both timestamps and two dispositions. The normative MIXED-NS-EXCHANGE also requires the byte-validated missing objects to carry synthetic MIXED-NS-1 IDs for which the fixture supplies no bytes; the exact combined synthetic-root exchange is not claimed. Section 5.3 lease derivation, divergent event union, a sync coordinator, and durable recovery are outside these entry points. |
+
